{'query': 'reputable peer-reviewed scientific source on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'A review of the global climate change impacts, adaptation ...', 'url': 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8978769/', 'snippet': 'This review aims to highlight the effects of climate change in a socio-scientific aspect by analyzing the existing literature on various sectorial pieces of evidence globally that influence the environment.'}, {'title': '(PDF) Understanding Climate Change: A Review of Causes ...', 'url': 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397706496_Understanding_Climate_Change_A_Review_of_Causes_Impacts_and_Responses', 'snippet': 'Nov 18, 2025 · This brief summarizes and analyzes the natural and human causes of the greenhouse effect, the existing scientific evidence, and the environmental, economic, and social impacts of climate...'}, {'title': 'Climate change and its environmental and health effects from ...', 'url': 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405844025006954', 'snippet': 'Feb 15, 2025 · This review seeks to investigate the far-reaching effects of climate change on health and the associated environmental consequences, both on a global scale and within the EMRO region.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change - Recent articles and discoveries - Springer', 'url': 'https://link.springer.com/subjects/climate-change', 'snippet': '2 days ago · Uncover the latest and most impactful research in Climate Change. Explore pioneering discoveries, insightful ideas and new methods from leading researchers in the field.'}, {'title': 'Articles | Nature Climate Change', 'url': 'https://www.nature.com/nclimate/articles?type=article', 'snippet': '4 days ago · Here researchers find that climate change may intensify such events across wind, solar and compound forms. Climate discourse is often misjudged, yet the mechanisms remain unclear.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 7.696206099994015}
{'query': 'government or international body report on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change - Wikipedia', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intergovernmental_Panel_on_Climate_Change', 'snippet': "The report also shows how adaptation to the effects of climate change can reduce some of its ill effects. The IPCC's Fourth Assessment Report (AR4) was published in 2007."}, {'title': 'Climate Reports | United Nations - الأمم المتحدة', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/climatechange/reports', 'snippet': 'Jun 23, 2026 · The report “Climate Action and Support Trends” was prepared as UN Climate Change input to the UN Climate Action Summit, and it puts a spotlight on the progress made over the past 25 years...'}, {'title': 'IPCC — Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'url': 'https://www.ipcc.ch/', 'snippet': 'Through its assessments, the IPCC determines the state of knowledge on climate change. It identifies where there is agreement in the scientific community on topics related to climate change, and where further research is needed. The reports are drafted and reviewed in several stages, thus guaranteeing objectivity and transparency.'}, {'title': 'Major Reports - Climate Change - A Global Issue - Research ...', 'url': 'https://research.un.org/en/climate-change/reports', 'snippet': 'Oct 22, 2025 · Since 2017, the Yearbook of Global Climate Action reviews the state and scope of climate action worldwide.'}, {'title': 'Reports — IPCC', 'url': 'https://www.ipcc.ch/reports/', 'snippet': 'The IPCC prepares comprehensive Assessment Reports about knowledge on climate change, its causes, potential impacts and response options. The IPCC also produces Special Reports, which are an assessment on a specific issue and Methodology Reports, which provide practical guidelines for the preparation of greenhouse gas inventories.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 2.768764199980069}
{'query': 'global average temperatures trend 2023 2024 latest data', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate change: global temperature | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-global-temperature', 'snippet': 'Yearly surface temperature from 1880–2024 compared to the 20th-century average (1901-2000). Blue bars indicate cooler-than-average years; red bars show warmer-than-average years. NOAA Climate.gov graph, based on data from the National Centers for Environmental Information.'}, {'title': 'Global Temperature - Earth Indicator - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/earth/explore/earth-indicators/global-temperature/', 'snippet': 'Global temperatures in 2025 were cooler than 2024, with average temperatures of 2.14 degrees Fahrenheit (1.19 degrees Celsius) above the 1951 to 1980 average. The data shown are the latest available, updated annually.'}, {'title': 'Winter 2023/2024 is starting to trend colder in the latest forecast, with...', 'url': 'https://www.severe-weather.eu/long-range-2/winter-2023-2024-forecast-polar-vortex-el-nino-qbo-strong-impact-cold-weather-united-states-canada-europe-fa/', 'snippet': 'Latest Winter forecast data shows a colder trend emerging for the United States, powered by the El Nino, Polar Vortex and the QBO anomaly.'}, {'title': 'Climate Pulse - Near real-time updates of global climate variables', 'url': 'https://pulse.climate.copernicus.eu/', 'snippet': 'Surface air temperature anomaly. Baseline: 1991-2020 Data: ERA5. Credit: C3S/ECMWF. Climate Pulse provides near real-time updates of key global climate variables from the Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S).'}, {'title': 'Global warming | Definition, Causes, Effects, Solutions... | Britannica', 'url': 'https://www.britannica.com/science/global-warming', 'snippet': 'Global warming, the phenomenon of increasing average air temperatures near Earth’s surface over the past one to two centuries, happens mostly in the troposphere, the lowest level of the atmosphere, which extends from Earth’s surface up to a height of 6–11 miles.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 6.568309800000861}
